0,Tanosy dialect - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanosy_dialect,"Tanosy is spoken in the Anosy region, especially in the Taolanaro District, and is the primary dialect spoken in the city of Fort-Dauphin. [6] A community of Tanosy emigrés also exists in Bezaha, located in Atsimo-Andrefana, where their dialect is influenced by neighboring Mahafaly and Bara.","Malagasy, Tanosy",Austronesian
1,Music of Madagascar - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Madagascar,"Music in Madagascar tends toward major keys and diatonic scales, [6] although coastal music makes frequent use of minor keys, most likely due to early Arab influences at coastal ports of call. [7] Malagasy music has served a wide range of social, spiritual and mundane functions across the centuries.","Malagasy, Tanosy",Austronesian
