5,"Malagasy cultural resources: podcasts, films, music | Targumi",https://www.targumi.com/en/cultural-resources/malgache,"Malagasy cultural resources Malagasy is the language of a unique island-continent. Madagascar offers a fascinating culture blending Austronesian, African, Arab and French traditions. From salegy music to the growing Malagasy film industry and educational YouTube channels, here is our selection to discover Malagasy culture through immersion.","Malagasy, Tanosy",Austronesian
6,Music of Madagascar — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Music_of_Madagascar,"The music of Madagascar comprises the diverse traditional and contemporary styles performed by the Malagasy people, reflecting the island's settlement by Austronesian migrants from Southeast Asia around the 5th to 10th centuries CE and subsequent Bantu arrivals from East Africa, which produced a distinctive synthesis of melodic chordophones and rhythmic percussion. [1][2] Traditional Malagasy ...","Malagasy, Tanosy",Austronesian
